# fixedbugs, defect 560, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R3; the
# sitting's `fp`, with tests).
#
# Two modules each bind a `static inline twice` from a header of their own,
# one of `long long` and one of `int`. `build` compiles a unit per module and
# prints 6 and 8. Until 2026-10-10 `heroes test` compiled the whole program
# as one unit, where the two `twice` are one name declared two ways, and
# refused it. It compiles a unit per module now, the root's carrying the
# runner of every module's tests, and the program's `main` never runs before
# them.
use fixedbugs560/long_twice
use fixedbugs560/int_twice

function main()
    print(long_twice.doubled(x: 3))
    print(int_twice.doubled(x: 4))

test "both modules double"
    assert long_twice.doubled(x: 1) == 2
    assert int_twice.doubled(x: 2) == 4
